/// Latency benchmark for the golden text index.
///
///     greycat run goldenTextBench::bench
///
/// Two things are deliberate about the shape of this file.
///
/// **Every case carries the row the client meant** (`GoldenBenchCase.want`), and the
/// table reports the RANK that row came back at. Latency alone would rank a wrong answer
/// first: the cheapest response of all is a confident page of wrong rows. `rank=0` means
/// the wanted row is not in the top k — a miss, however fast it was.
///
/// **It prints with `println`.** The logger is the rule elsewhere in this project, but
/// its lines go to the log file and never to the terminal; a benchmark whose whole output
/// is a table to read is the one-off CLI dump `println` is for. Each case also emits one
/// machine-readable `BENCH,` CSV line, so two configurations can be diffed with `diff`
/// instead of by eye.
///
/// Every case runs `reps` times (default 3) and all runs are printed, because the spread
/// between the first and the rest IS the cache effect and averaging it away hides which
/// queries are cache-sensitive.

/// One benchmark query, tagged by what it exercises.
@volatile
type GoldenBenchCase {
    /// What the query is meant to represent, e.g. "typo sole word".
    name: String;
    query: String;
    /// A string that must appear in the indexed body of the row the client meant.
    want: String;
}

/// The query set. Both rows are real addresses in the store:
///
///     4 Avenue de la Gare, 1610 Luxembourg      (uid WmCPos)
///     8 Elterstrachen, 7260 Bereldange          (uid DbbsDL, commune Walferdange)
///     5 Rue de l'Industrie, 1811 Luxembourg     (uid FazGB4)
///
/// The set walks the shapes a client actually types: a whole address, progressively less
/// of it, an abbreviation, a postcode alone, and the two kinds of typo — one wrong word
/// among several, and a sole wrong word with nothing else to carry the query.
///
/// `number + typo` is the hardest case in the set and the one that exercises the most of
/// the config at once: a bare house number, no town, and a street word that is both
/// misspelled AND elided. It only resolves if the apostrophe fold in
/// `GoldenTextSearch::tokenization` put "lindustrie" and "l'industrie" in the same term
/// AND typo tolerance reaches "industrie" from "industrye" — and the "5" carries almost
/// no weight, since every street has one.
///
/// The `typing ...` cases are one address typed a character at a time and are the reason
/// `searchTypeahead` exists: under plain BM25 every one of them reduced to the single term
/// "5" and returned the same tied rows until the last keystroke.
///
/// Four cases are known rank-0 or rank-poor, and each is kept to document a real limit
/// rather than to be quietly fixed:
///
///   `commune only`    Walferdange commune holds many streets; BM25 returns twenty of
///                     them and the Elterstrachen row is not among them. Correct for a
///                     query naming no street — hits > 0 and "found what was meant" are
///                     different questions.
///   `elision omitted` "5 rue de lindus" — the client typed neither the apostrophe nor a
///                     space, so the fragment is "lindus" and the indexed term is
///                     "industrie". This is the exact cost of the charMap rule in
///                     `GoldenTextSearch::tokenization`, priced in a test.
///   `noise word`      "zzzeldange" returns Bereldange. It is what `maxEdits2: 3` buys and
///                     is here so nobody raises the budget again without seeing it.
///   `abbreviated`     "av de la gare luxembourg" — NOT a config problem. Some golden
///                     street names are stored abbreviated ("av. Grand Duc Jean"), so "av"
///                     is a genuine and RARE vocabulary term while "avenue" is very common.
///                     BM25 weights the abbreviation far above the word it abbreviates, and
///                     the synonym cannot correct it because synonyms carry no weight. Fix
///                     it in the data or with a weighted expansion, not with a knob.
fn cases(): Array<GoldenBenchCase> {
    var gare = "Avenue de la Gare";
    var elter = "Elterstrachen";
    var indus = "Rue de l'Industrie";
    return Array<GoldenBenchCase> {
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "full address", query: "4 Avenue de la Gare, 1610 Luxembourg", want: gare },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "number + street", query: "4 avenue de la gare luxembourg", want: gare },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "street + town", query: "avenue de la gare luxembourg", want: gare },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "street only", query: "avenue de la gare", want: gare },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "abbreviated", query: "av de la gare luxembourg", want: gare },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "postcode only", query: "1610", want: gare },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "postcode + town", query: "7260 bereldange", want: elter },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "street + town 2", query: "elterstrachen bereldange", want: elter },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "town only", query: "bereldange", want: elter },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "commune only", query: "walferdange", want: elter },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "typo one word", query: "elterstrahen bereldange", want: elter },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "typo sole word", query: "bereldanje", want: elter },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "typo street", query: "avenue de la garre luxembourg", want: gare },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "word prefix", query: "bereldang", want: elter },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "number + typo", query: "5 industrye", want: indus },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "transposed typo", query: "5 indsutrye", want: indus },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "typing 5 i", query: "5 i", want: indus },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "typing 5 ind", query: "5 ind", want: indus },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "typing 5 indus", query: "5 indus", want: indus },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "typing 5 industr", query: "5 industr", want: indus },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "typing full elided", query: "5 rue de l'indus", want: indus },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "elision omitted", query: "5 rue de lindus", want: indus },
        GoldenBenchCase { name: "noise word", query: "zzzeldange", want: elter },
    };
}

/// Milliseconds, two decimals.
fn ms(us: int): String {
    return float::to_string((us as float) / 1000.0, '.', null, 2, false);
}

/// Appends `v` truncated-or-padded to `w` characters, then one space.
fn col(b: Buffer, v: any?, w: int) {
    b.add_and_pad(v, w, ' ');
    b.add(" ");
}

/// 1-based position of the first row whose indexed body carries `want`, or 0 when the
/// wanted row is not in the results at all.
///
/// Called after the clock is read, never inside the timed window.
fn rank_of(rows: Array<TextResult>, want: String): int {
    var needle = want.lowercase();
    for (var i = 0; i < rows.size(); i++) {
        var nPoi = rows[i].value as node<GoldenPointOfInterest>?;
        if (nPoi != null) {
            if (GoldenTextSearch::docText(nPoi).lowercase().contains(needle)) {
                return i + 1;
            }
        }
    }
    return 0;
}

/// Runs the shipped search — `searchTypeahead`, the exact call `searchAddress` makes —
/// `reps` times per query, and prints hits, the rank of the wanted row, every run's
/// milliseconds and the best of them.
fn bench(k: int?, reps: int?) {
    var kk = k ?? 20;
    var n = reps ?? 3;
    var idx = GoldenTextSearch::require();

    // One warm-up so the library's lazily-built cached maps are not billed to whichever
    // case happens to run first.
    GoldenTextSearch::searchTypeahead(idx, "warmup", kk);

    var s = idx.stats();
    println("");
    println("golden text index benchmark  k=${kk} reps=${n}");
    println(
        "docs=${s.totalEntries} terms=${s.totalTerms} avgTokens=${float::to_string(s.avgTokenCount, '.', null, 2, false)}"
    );
    println("");

    var head = Buffer {};
    col(head, "case", 16);
    col(head, "query", 38);
    col(head, "hits", 4);
    col(head, "rank", 4);
    for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        col(head, "run${i + 1}", 8);
    }
    col(head, "best", 8);
    println(head.toString());

    var cs = cases();
    for (var ci = 0; ci < cs.size(); ci++) {
        var c = cs[ci];
        var runs = Array<int> {};
        var hits = 0;
        var rank = 0;

        for (var r = 0; r < n; r++) {
            var t0 = time::now().to(DurationUnit::microseconds);
            var rows = GoldenTextSearch::searchTypeahead(idx, c.query, kk);
            var t1 = time::now().to(DurationUnit::microseconds);
            runs.add(t1 - t0);
            hits = rows.size();
            rank = rank_of(rows, c.want);
        }

        var best = runs[0];
        for (var i = 1; i < runs.size(); i++) {
            if (runs[i] < best) {
                best = runs[i];
            }
        }

        var line = Buffer {};
        col(line, c.name, 16);
        col(line, c.query, 38);
        col(line, hits, 4);
        col(line, rank, 4);
        for (var i = 0; i < runs.size(); i++) {
            col(line, ms(runs[i]), 8);
        }
        col(line, ms(best), 8);
        println(line.toString());
        println("BENCH,${c.name},${c.query},${hits},${rank},${ms(best)}");
    }
}

/// Diagnostic for one query: its tokens, what plain BM25 returns, what the last token
/// completes to, and what a prefix pass on it returns.
///
///     greycat run goldenTextBench::probe "av de la gare luxembourg"
///
/// The bench tells you a case regressed; this tells you why. Both findings below came
/// out of it and neither was visible from a rank column.
fn probe(q: String) {
    var idx = GoldenTextSearch::require();
    var toks = TextTokenizer::tokenize(q, idx.config);
    var b = Buffer {};
    for (var i = 0; i < toks.size(); i++) {
        if (i > 0) { b.add(" | "); }
        b.add(toks[i].text);
    }
    println("query '${q}' tokens: ${b.toString()}");

    var last = toks[toks.size() - 1].text;
    var bm = GoldenTextSearch::search(idx, q, 5);
    println("  bm25 -> ${bm.size()} hits");
    for (var i = 0; i < bm.size(); i++) {
        println("    [${float::to_string(bm[i].score, '.', null, 3, false)}] ${bm[i].text}");
    }
    var sug = idx.suggest(last, 10);
    var sb = Buffer {};
    for (var i = 0; i < sug.size(); i++) {
        if (i > 0) { sb.add(", "); }
        sb.add("${sug[i].term}(df=${sug[i].df})");
    }
    println("  suggest('${last}') -> ${sug.size()}: ${sb.toString()}");

    var pre = idx.search_prefix(last, 5);
    println("  prefix('${last}') -> ${pre.size()} hits");
    for (var i = 0; i < pre.size(); i++) {
        println("    [${float::to_string(pre[i].score, '.', null, 3, false)}] ${pre[i].text}");
    }
}
